# Build output. Builds do NOT live in the tree: the presets put them in $DEVSYSTEM_BUILDTREES and installs in
# $DEVSYSTEM_DEPLOYS. These stay as a guard against a manual out-of-preset configure landing here.
build/
/build*/

# Personal CMake presets. Machine-specific by definition, so never tracked -- a committed one with an absolute
# toolchain path breaks for everyone the moment that path changes. Start from CMakeUserPresets.json.example.
CMakeUserPresets.json

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
*.cmake.user

# Qt Creator
*.user
*.user.*
.qtcreator/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.autosave
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Vendor reference material, kept at the repository root for consultation but NOT tracked: the ZWO SDK's own demo
# application (19 MB, and it bundles OpenCV binaries this library deliberately does not depend on) and its PDF
# documentation. Only the SDK BUILD PAYLOAD lives under DegorasASI/thirdparty/ASI/ and is tracked, mirroring how the
# reference project vendors thirdparty/Thorlabs/. Re-populate this directory from the official SDK download if needed.
reference/

# Capture output the examples write to their WORKING DIRECTORY.
#
# Every example that grabs a frame writes it beside wherever it was launched from, so running one from the
# repository root drops a few megabytes of .pgm and .bmp into the source tree. Six of them reached a commit
# that way -- 13.8 MB -- which is what this exists to stop. Launch the examples from their build directory and
# the files land there instead, which is where they belong.
asi_frame_*.pgm
asi_frame_*.bmp
asi_stream_*.bmp
shot.bmp
